"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.7.rc3.official [645638db9]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.rc3 - Ubuntu 26.04 LTS 26.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon Vega 10 Graphics (radeonsi, raven, ACO, DRM 3.64, 7.0.0-22-generic) - AMD Ryzen 7 3750H with Radeon Vega Mobile Gfx (8 threads) - 13.59 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm messing with Blender in order to see why I can't get the lighting to the look similar, and while messing with the values, Blender produced Inner & Outer values that were similar.\n\n<img width=\"445\" height=\"273\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ee48c0b-0e7f-44cc-ae3b-9188c9c728a2\" />\n\nThis causes the light to disappear in Godot, and i get this error.\n\n<img width=\"981\" height=\"184\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/26537d2b-5121-4d8d-a41f-2904c51110ac\" />\n\nWith lowering the inner values...\n\n```\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"innerConeAngle\":0.08968102931976317,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"outerConeAngle\":0.08968102931976318\n```\n\n❌ Error still shows.\n\n```\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"innerConeAngle\":0.089681029,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"outerConeAngle\":0.08968102931976318\n```\n❌ Error still comes up.\n\n\n```\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"innerConeAngle\":0.08968102,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"outerConeAngle\":0.08968102931976318\n```\n✅ No error!\n\nI do have this on the light though, but I'm not sure if this is related to this issue.\n<img width=\"340\" height=\"49\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d42e5314-c127-48f3-b982-3c4e4599c714\" />\n\nI mainly care about this issue, because I'm wondering why this is happening, when the code just checks if something is greater than another number.\nPlus, I wonder how many times I'm messing with something in blender, and then the light disappears and doesn't show up in Godot, and I never even knew why.\n\n\nFor anyone curious, the light looked light this.\nAgain, I'm just playing around with the values to see what does and doesn't get sent from Blender to Godot, and when and where the lighting doesn't match.\n\n<img width=\"643\" height=\"797\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/00df38d2-0f0c-49b0-a1eb-5859326f08f1\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMake a spot light in a gltf file where the values for innerConeAngle & outerConeAngle are very close to each other.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nHere's a \"minimal reproduction\" scene that I'm using to test it.\nLet me know if you have troubles figuring it out. :P\n\n[gltf_light_testing_desert_level.tar.gz](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29077506/gltf_light_testing_desert_level.tar.gz)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120387/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120387/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}